From 1a15c411eae640d6e44d483077dc1bd347c8418a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Steere <marksteere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:36:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add Yonkoma (experimental)

Yonkoma by Mark Steere (October 2026): two red and two blue checkers on
a 10x10 or 12x12 checkerboard.  A checker moves along a diagonal like a
bishop; every move must lower the sum of the moved checker's king-move
distances to the two enemy checkers, or keep that sum and take the
checker farther from its partner.  Whoever completes a crosscut (a 2x2
block holding all four checkers) loses.  A player with no legal move
has the turn skipped (autopass).

- src/games/yonkoma.ts: rules, click handling with the legal
  destinations shown while a move is entered, a felt-and-oak board
  with glazed ceramic checkers drawn as custom glyphs (glyphDefs) and a
  plain-board alternative display, custom default colours, structured
  chat line for the crosscut ending.
- test/games/yonkoma.test.ts: rule-sheet figures, a full game with a
  skipped turn, click handling, chat log parity, render contracts,
  seeded random play on both boards.
- English strings merged into the locale files; CHANGELOG entry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
